From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:50:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: apple: Accept idle rails under 0.1 W

The power work treats a reading of less than 0.1 W across the P-CPU,
E-CPU and GPU rails as a firmware reset image: it reports -ENODATA,
retains the minimum CPU and GPU ceilings and fails the hwmon rails with
-EAGAIN. An idle J713 reads below that once its GPU idles at a low
performance state (P-CPU 40-55 mW, E-CPU 9 mW, GPU 27 mW): the
ceilings then sat at the minimum while idle, the CPUs ran at 900 MHz,
and the GPU budget climbed back one state at a time once work arrived.

A reset image reads zero on both CPU rails, which the running reader
cannot. Reject only that.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 20d757d2b41c0932ef91c41afd97e3ddfdbbf64b)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c b/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
index 81b7bb6093..203ea9f560 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/apple-pmp-thermal.c
@@ -174,10 +174,11 @@ static void apple_pmp_power_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	u64 epoch = apple_pmp_gpu_epoch(pmp_thermal.sensors);
 	u64 now;
 	int ret = apple_pmp_power_read_rails(mw);
-	/* The running CPUs/reader cannot plausibly consume <0.1 W in total.
-	 * A firmware reset/all-zero image must not refill the energy bucket.
+	/* The running reader cannot read zero on both CPU rails. A firmware
+	 * reset/all-zero image must not refill the energy bucket; an idle
+	 * system may still draw well under 0.1 W on all three rails.
 	 */
-	if (!ret && mw[0] + mw[1] + mw[2] < 100)
+	if (!ret && !mw[0] && !mw[1])
 		ret = -ENODATA;
 	/* Clock under the lock: a raw sample published while the SMC reads ran
 	 * must not make the unsigned age below wrap into a false -EAGAIN.
